# Upstream sources and the tag every tool in the suite pins.
#
# This file is the single place a tag is chosen. Bumping one here and
# regenerating (tools/make_registry.sh) moves every tool at once -- which is the
# point: kycg pinned InfiniumAnnotation v8 while sesame-cli pinned v8.1, so the
# two of them could not share a download even though they consume the identical
# files.
#
# A tag is only half of a pin. The other half is sha256(SHA256SUMS) per
# directory, which is NOT written here: it is computed from the cached upstream
# manifests under sums/<source>/<tag>/, so a pin can never disagree with the
# bytes it claims to describe. Adding a tag means caching its manifests:
#
#   curl -sfL -o sums/InfiniumAnnotation/<tag>/<platform>/SHA256SUMS \
#     https://github.com/zhou-lab/InfiniumAnnotation/raw/<tag>/<platform>/SHA256SUMS
#
# source              tag     base_url
InfiniumAnnotation    v8.1    https://github.com/zhou-lab/InfiniumAnnotation/raw
genomes               v3      https://github.com/zhou-lab/genomes/raw
KYCGKB                v2      https://github.com/zhou-lab
methscope             v3      https://raw.githubusercontent.com/zhou-lab/methscope_data
methscope_models      v4      https://huggingface.co/zhou-lab/methscope/resolve
